# Reproducibility (v2 pipeline)

`python reproduce_all.py` from the project root runs: smoke tests → monthly panel from data/raw → intra-month MIDAS blocks →
all nowcast designs/samples/models (origin-wise SHAP) → MIDAS benchmarks → evaluation (DM-HLN, MCS)
→ robustness (hyperparameters, windows, collinearity) → figures. Every number in the manuscript
comes from `results/` produced by this command in the environment recorded in
`results/environment_report.txt`; `requirements.txt` pins those versions.

Determinism: XGBoost uses `tree_method="exact"` with `n_jobs=1` and LightGBM uses
`deterministic=True, force_row_wise=True, n_jobs=1`. Elastic Net, Ridge, the naive and MIDAS
benchmarks are deterministic by construction. Cross-platform agreement of the tree models under
these settings is reported in `results/reproduction_summary.txt` (compare Windows and Linux runs).

Design vocabulary used throughout:
- `conditional`   nowcast conditional on the same-month headline CPI release (includes `headline_mom`)
- `unconditional` real-time nowcast using only information available before the CPI release
- `core` / `extended`  without / with the 12-month inflation-expectations block

Figure note: `fig_dominant_counts` in `src/figures/make_figures.py` ignores forecast origins at which the
Elastic Net selects no variable (two origins in the extended sample); earlier versions assigned such
origins to the alphabetically first family.
